[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32971"] :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(2,-5,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-5,3⟩,$ and $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =⟨2,-5,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-70647/selection/73526bd143442a71233eb52139781153dd628070b77095433ca990c24d7b7b1e" :answer/id #uuid "0a31383c-ff79-5565-90a9-06ed987e7c20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70647/selection/0b863d6e1ed32771f4f0bec37f3697b2aa4fbfdc0c546ed5b09a803ff3cd80fd" :answer/id #uuid "364eac3b-e0ca-5f00-867e-8707462b7cc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70647/selection/cfd7913ed9a8246f0e276514faec36648c1e9c6ec10087e2a2d26ec44923c9c9" :answer/id #uuid "7329a3d9-cbe9-5c7d-a9d2-2c2a2bda2f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70647/selection/b1fdee68cf2ce1b291dc9683299ae9239aea76a55e3547280afbc4eebd02f082" :answer/id #uuid "424550e6-88ec-5364-9608-4cb87b21b87c" :answer/type :a